# The deployable artifact is static-demo/, and it is deployed from inside that
# directory. Running `vercel deploy` from the repository root instead builds
# the Python app as a second Vercel project, which is how a stray `rag-project`
# deployment came to exist on 2026-08-30.
#
# Vercel falls back to .gitignore only when this file is absent, and that
# fallback did not hold: 826 of 913 files went up, including gitignored
# directories. So the secret is excluded here explicitly rather than left to a
# fallback, and first, because it is the line that matters.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem

# Everything a root deploy has no business uploading.
.venv/
node_modules/
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The corpora and the built indexes: third-party documents, and the same text
# again inside metadata.json.
data/
data-birds/
data-quant/
vector_store/
store-birds/
store-quant/
runs/
archive/

# The recorded build deploys itself, from its own directory.
static-demo/
